.\" bnrmr(1) - BannerManor. Keep in step with print_usage (src/cli.cyr);
.\" tests/bannermanor.tcyr checks that every flag appears here.
.TH BNRMR 1 2026-10-15 "BannerManor 1.8.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bnrmr \- render text as an ASCII-art banner
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bnrmr
.RI [ flags ]
.I text
\&...
.br
.B bnrmr
.B \-\-list\-fonts
.br
.B bnrmr
.BR \-\-help " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bnrmr
writes
.I text
to standard output as a banner of
.B #
characters, one font row per output line.
The words of
.I text
are joined with single spaces;
the joined text may be at most 1024 bytes.
It renders and exits: no configuration file, no daemon, no cache.
.PP
Fonts are CYML files (BannerManor's own format) or legacy figlet
.B .flf
files.
Without
.BR \-\-font ,
the built-in
.B block
font is used, so
.B bnrmr
needs no files at all.
.PP
Printable ASCII (space through
.BR ~ )
renders.
Lowercase letters fold to uppercase when the font has no lowercase glyphs.
Any other byte, including every byte of a multi-byte UTF-8 character,
renders as the font's blank glyph.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-font " \fINAME\fR"
Use font
.IR NAME ,
found on the font search path (see
.BR FONTS ).
.I NAME
may not contain
.BR / ,
.BR \e ,
.B .
or a control character, and is at most 64 bytes.
A value ending in
.B .flf
is instead the path of a figlet font, used as given.
.TP
.BI \-\-align " WHERE"
.BR left " (default), " center " or " right ;
also
.BR L ", " C ", " R " and " centre .
Alignment is within the frame: the
.B \-\-width
value if given, else the terminal's width, else
.BR $COLUMNS ,
else 80.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-width " \fIN\fR"
Draw only the glyphs that fit in
.I N
columns, cutting at a glyph boundary.
0 (the default) means no limit.
At most 4096.
A width narrower than one glyph draws blank rows.
Without
.BR \-\-width ,
output to a terminal is cut to the terminal's width;
output to a pipe or file is not.
.TP
.BI \-\-pad " N"
Write
.I N
blank lines above and below the banner (default 0, at most 64).
.TP
.BI \-\-color " NAME"
Color each row:
.BR black ", " red ", " green ", " yellow ", " blue ", " magenta ,
.BR cyan ", " white ,
their
.BI bright_ name
or
.BI bright\- name
forms, or
.B rainbow
for a different color per row.
Color is written only when standard output is a terminal;
in a pipe or file the bytes are plain.
On AGNOS only the console counts as a terminal,
here and for the width cut under
.BR \-\-width .
.TP
.B \-\-list\-fonts
List the fonts
.B \-\-font
can find: name, glyph size, gap and description.
Files that fail to load, or whose names
.B \-\-font
cannot spell, are listed as skipped.
The last line names the directories searched.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a summary of the flags and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
End of flags: everything after it is text, even a word that starts with
.BR \- .
.PP
Long flags take their value as the next word or after
.BR = ;
flags may come before or after the text.
Short flags cannot be bundled
.RB ( \-hf ),
and a short flag's value is the next word
.RB ( "\-w 20" ,
not
.BR \-w20 ).
.SH FONTS
.B \-\-font
.I NAME
looks for
.IB NAME .cyml
in these places, in order, and uses the first that exists:
.IP 1. 4
the directory named by
.BR $BNRMR_FONTS ,
if it is set and not empty;
.IP 2. 4
.BR ./fonts ,
relative to the current directory;
.IP 3. 4
.IR prefix /share/bannermanor/fonts ,
when
.B bnrmr
itself is
.IR prefix /bin/bnrmr ,
as it is after
.B scripts/install.sh
or in an unpacked release archive;
.IP 4. 4
for
.B block
only, the built-in copy.
.PP
The first file found is the font even if it fails to load:
a broken font is an error that names the file,
never a silent fall-back to another font of the same name.
.PP
The fonts shipped with BannerManor are
.B block
(5\(mu5),
.B slim
(4\(mu5),
.B big
(7\(mu7) and
.B clean
(7\(mu8).
Only
.B clean
has lowercase letters; the others draw them as capitals.
.B clean
is Dale Schumacher's X11 bitmap font Clean, under its own permissive
license, which the font file reproduces.
A figlet font may be at most 1 MB and its glyphs at most
128 columns by 64 rows.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BNRMR_FONTS
A directory searched before
.BR ./fonts .
It must be under 1024 bytes and contain no control characters;
any other value is an error when a font is looked up.
.TP
.B COLUMNS
The frame width for
.B \-\-align
when standard output is not a terminal and
.B \-\-width
is not given.
Values above 4096 count as 4096.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The banner, listing, help or version was written.
.TP
.B 1
Anything else: an unknown or malformed flag, a font that is not found or
does not load, text over 1024 bytes, more than 255 arguments, or a write to
standard output that failed (a full disk, a closed descriptor).
.PP
Diagnostics go to standard error, so
.RB \(dq bnrmr " ... > " file \(dq
never writes an error message into
.IR file .
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
bnrmr AGNOS
bnrmr \-\-font slim \-\-align center "Welcome home"
bnrmr \-\-font clean "Welcome home"
bnrmr \-\-color rainbow \-\-font big HI
bnrmr \-\-font ./standard.flf hello
bnrmr \-\- \-5 C
bnrmr \-\-font big "$(hostname)" > /etc/motd
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.IB prefix /share/bannermanor/fonts/*.cyml
The installed fonts.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR figlet (6)
.PP
The font format:
.I docs/adr/0001\-cyml\-font\-format.md
and
.I docs/guides/fonts.md
in the BannerManor source.
.SH BUGS
Report them at https://github.com/MacCracken/bannermanor/issues.
